  "$comment": "Star-data incident switch shared by apps/web (imported at build time via apps/web/lib/data-quality.ts) and packages/api-server (read from disk at startup via src/utils/data-quality.ts). Two independent GitHub-side changes degraded event-derived metrics: (1) since ~2025-05-23 the /events firehose is partitioned by position - offsets 1-100 are a ~97% PushEvent block and the healthy event mix only appears at offsets 101-300 (hard cap 300) - while our ETL polled only page 1, so star/PR/issue events were barely captured; (2) since ~2025-11 GitHub trims payload fields, so PR additions/deletions and push commit counts arrive as 0 (unknown, not zero). 'blocked' queries are rankings/leaderboards built on WatchEvent rows or star-event counts and must not be served while active=true; 'tainted' queries return event-derived series/counts that are lower bounds and are served with a data_quality marker attached. Flip active to false once the ETL reads pages 1-3 and the affected windows are re-materialized (or rankings move to stargazerCount snapshots).",
